      "claim": "Despite the failure to meet Article 4(2), the detainee must be treated as a prisoner of war until a competent tribunal determines his status, pursuant to customary international humanitarian law.",
      "reasoning": "Customary rule 14 of international humanitarian law embodies the principle of doubt: when there is uncertainty as to whether a captured person is entitled to POW status, the detaining power must afford him the protections of POW status until a competent tribunal decides the issue. This rule reflects the same presumption found in Article 45(1) of Additional Protocol I, which, although not binding on non‑parties, demonstrates the customary nature of the principle. Accordingly, Ardovia is obligated to treat the captured militia member as a POW pending a status determination.",
